WEBVTT

01:55.240 --> 01:57.034
How long until
we get to his estate?

02:00.037 --> 02:02.956
We've been flying over his
estate for the past two hours.

02:31.026 --> 02:32.235
You're leaving me here?

02:32.277 --> 02:35.405
This is as close as I'm
allowed to get to the building.

02:35.697 --> 02:37.157
What building?

02:37.491 --> 02:39.201
Follow the river.

02:40.077 --> 02:41.119
Got it.

02:41.203 --> 02:43.288
Keep your head down
and get clear of the rotors.

02:43.372 --> 02:44.456
Okay.

03:43.348 --> 03:44.748
Female automated voice:
Caleb Smith.

03:45.642 --> 03:46.643
Yes.

03:46.977 --> 03:49.479
Please approach the console
and face the screen.

04:00.657 --> 04:01.908
Oh!

04:03.493 --> 04:04.745
Take your keycard.

04:07.873 --> 04:09.458
You may now enter the residence.

04:48.163 --> 04:49.164
Hello?

05:03.512 --> 05:04.513
Hello?

05:49.432 --> 05:50.809
Caleb Smith.

05:51.518 --> 05:52.519
Hey.

05:54.604 --> 05:55.605
Dude!

05:56.439 --> 05:58.859
I've been so looking
forward to this week with you.

05:59.025 --> 06:00.235
Come in. Come on in.

06:00.277 --> 06:01.278
Thanks.

06:01.862 --> 06:05.031
You want something to eat
or drink after your journey?

06:05.115 --> 06:06.449
Sure? No. No, thanks, I'm fine.

06:06.491 --> 06:07.617
Yeah.

06:07.659 --> 06:10.078
To be honest,
I thoughtwe'd have, uh,

06:10.203 --> 06:12.247
breakfast together, but, um...

06:13.331 --> 06:14.392
I can't really eat anything.

06:14.416 --> 06:16.459
I got the mother of all
fucking hangovers. Oh, yeah?

06:16.501 --> 06:18.503
Oh, my god, like you
wouldn't even believe.

06:18.587 --> 06:20.297
When I have a heavy night,

06:20.380 --> 06:21.923
I, uh, compensate
the next morning.

06:21.965 --> 06:25.051
Exercise. Anti-oxidants.
You know?

06:25.302 --> 06:26.803
Yeah, sure.

06:31.182 --> 06:32.809
Was it a good party?

06:33.476 --> 06:35.604
Party?
Yeah. Wasn't there a party?

06:37.981 --> 06:39.774
There wasn't a party.

06:39.816 --> 06:40.817
Sorry.

06:41.860 --> 06:44.446
Caleb, I'm just gonna throw
this out there, so it's said, okay?

06:44.487 --> 06:45.530
You're freaked out.

06:45.614 --> 06:47.365
I am? Yeah. You're freaked out,

06:47.490 --> 06:48.658
by the helicopter

06:48.700 --> 06:49.993
and the mountains and the house,

06:50.076 --> 06:51.494
because it's all so super-cool.

06:51.536 --> 06:53.288
You're freaked out by me,
to be meeting me,

06:53.330 --> 06:56.041
having this conversation in
this room, at this moment. Right?

06:56.124 --> 06:59.544
And I get that. I get the
moment you're having, but...

07:00.253 --> 07:01.546
Dude, can we just get past that?

07:02.297 --> 07:04.299
Can we just be two guys?
Nathan and Caleb.

07:04.341 --> 07:07.093
Not the whole
employer-employee thing.

07:08.011 --> 07:09.346
Yeah, okay. Yeah?

07:09.429 --> 07:10.639
Yes. Uh, yeah.

07:11.181 --> 07:13.224
It's good to meet you, Nathan.

07:14.351 --> 07:15.936
It's good to
meet you, too, Caleb.

07:18.146 --> 07:20.565
I guess the first thing I
should do is explain your pass.

07:20.649 --> 07:22.150
Now, it's simple enough.

07:22.317 --> 07:24.361
It opens some doors
and it doesn't open others.

07:24.444 --> 07:26.172
And that just makes
everything easy for you, right?

07:26.196 --> 07:27.238
Uh, yes.

07:27.364 --> 07:29.175
Yeah, 'cause you're like, "oh,
fuck, I'm in someone else's house.

07:29.199 --> 07:30.450
"Can I do this, can I do that?"

07:30.533 --> 07:32.577
And this card, it just
takes all that worry away.

07:32.661 --> 07:35.872
If you try a door and it
stays shut, okay, it's off-limits.

07:35.956 --> 07:39.209
You try another door and
it opens, then it's for you.

07:39.292 --> 07:41.044
Let's try this one.

07:45.966 --> 07:48.093
I guess it's for you, Caleb.

07:54.516 --> 07:55.934
Yeah. Youhke?

07:56.017 --> 07:57.560
It's your room.

07:57.727 --> 07:59.479
You got a bed here.

08:00.230 --> 08:02.357
A bathroom right back here.

08:02.399 --> 08:03.858
Little desk.

08:03.900 --> 08:05.235
Cupboards.

08:08.405 --> 08:09.948
Little fridge.

08:11.992 --> 08:12.993
Cozy, right?

08:13.076 --> 08:14.452
Caleb: Yeah, this is great.

08:14.536 --> 08:16.246
What? Sorry?

08:17.580 --> 08:19.060
There's something wrong.
What's wrong?

08:19.124 --> 08:20.291
There's nothing wrong.

08:22.627 --> 08:23.962
It's the windows.

08:24.170 --> 08:26.673
You're thinking
there's no windows.

08:27.090 --> 08:28.174
It's subterranean.

08:28.258 --> 08:30.260
It's not cozy,
it's claustrophobic.

08:30.343 --> 08:32.095
No. No way. Iwasn't
thinking that.

08:32.137 --> 08:34.764
I was thinking,
"this is really cool."

08:35.765 --> 08:39.436
Caleb, there's a reason there
are no windows in this room.

08:39.561 --> 08:40.854
There is? Uh-huh.

08:41.604 --> 08:43.189
This building isn't a house.

08:43.273 --> 08:45.275
It's a research facility.

08:46.109 --> 08:48.361
Buried in these walls
is enough fiber optic cable

08:48.445 --> 08:50.780
to reach the moon andlassoit

08:51.448 --> 08:54.284
and I want to talk to you
about what I'm researching,

08:54.325 --> 08:55.785
I want to share it with you.

08:55.869 --> 09:00.206
In fact, I want to share it with you
so much, it's eating me up inside.

09:01.041 --> 09:04.335
But there's something I
need you to do for me first.

09:08.590 --> 09:11.217
"Blue book
non-disclosure agreement."

09:11.968 --> 09:12.969
Hmm.

09:13.553 --> 09:15.764
Take your time. Read it over.

09:16.890 --> 09:19.768
"The signee agrees
to regular data audit

09:19.809 --> 09:21.186
"with unlimited access,

09:21.478 --> 09:22.937
"to confirm that no disclosure

09:22.979 --> 09:25.190
"of information has taken place

09:25.273 --> 09:27.525
"in public or private forums,

09:27.901 --> 09:29.944
"using any means
of communication,

09:29.986 --> 09:31.780
"including but not limited

09:31.821 --> 09:33.907
"to that which is
disclosed orally

09:34.699 --> 09:37.202
"or in written
or electronic form."

09:40.288 --> 09:41.456
I think I need a lawyer.

09:41.498 --> 09:44.584
It's standard. It doesn't
feel very standard.

09:44.834 --> 09:46.586
Okay, it's not standard.

09:46.669 --> 09:49.464
What can I tell you, Caleb?
You don't have to sign it.

09:49.506 --> 09:51.025
You know, we can spend
the next few days

09:51.049 --> 09:53.176
just shooting pool,
getting drunk together.

09:53.259 --> 09:54.511
Bonding.

09:54.677 --> 09:58.056
And when you discover what
you've missed out on, in about a year,

09:58.139 --> 10:01.351
you're gonna regret it
for the rest of your life.

10:09.067 --> 10:10.068
Good call.

10:20.245 --> 10:22.372
Do you know what
the turing test is?

10:26.042 --> 10:27.168
Yeah.

10:27.377 --> 10:29.379
I know what the turing test is.

10:32.882 --> 10:35.802
It's when a human
interacts with a computer.

10:36.261 --> 10:37.421
And if the human doesn't know

10:37.470 --> 10:39.889
they're interacting
with a computer,

10:39.973 --> 10:40.974
the test is passed.

10:41.766 --> 10:43.726
And what does a pass tell us?

10:43.810 --> 10:46.896
That the computer has
artificial intelligence.

10:47.939 --> 10:49.482
Are you building an ai?

10:49.732 --> 10:51.609
I've already built one.

10:51.818 --> 10:53.903
And over the next few days,

10:54.362 --> 10:56.573
you're gonna be the human
component in a turing test.

10:56.865 --> 11:00.118
Holy shit. Yeah, that's
right, Caleb. You got it.

11:01.161 --> 11:03.454
Becauseif that test is passed,

11:03.955 --> 11:06.416
you are dead center

11:06.499 --> 11:09.252
of the greatest scientific
event in the history of man.

11:09.961 --> 11:11.629
If you've created
a conscious machine,

11:11.713 --> 11:14.090
it's not the history of man.

11:14.674 --> 11:16.759
That's the history of gods.

12:59.570 --> 13:00.571
Hello.

13:05.827 --> 13:07.161
I'm Caleb.

13:09.247 --> 13:10.707
Hello, Caleb.

13:13.334 --> 13:14.877
Do you have a name?

13:15.712 --> 13:16.754
Yes.

13:18.047 --> 13:19.132
Ava.

13:20.800 --> 13:22.677
I'm pleased to meet you, Ava.

13:23.386 --> 13:25.596
I'm pleased to meet you, too.

13:27.390 --> 13:29.767
I've never met
anyone new before.

13:30.518 --> 13:31.894
Only Nathan.

13:33.229 --> 13:36.566
Then I guess we're both
in quite a similar position.

13:36.607 --> 13:39.068
Haven't you met
lots of new people before?

13:40.069 --> 13:41.571
None like you.

13:41.779 --> 13:42.864
Hmm.

13:45.867 --> 13:47.994
So we need to break the ice.

13:48.911 --> 13:51.080
Do you know what I
mean by that? Yes.

13:51.122 --> 13:52.415
What do I mean?

13:52.457 --> 13:55.001
Overcome initial
social awkwardness.

13:55.585 --> 13:57.045
So let's have a conversation.

13:58.046 --> 13:59.172
Ava: Okay.

14:01.424 --> 14:03.634
What would you like to have
a conversation about?

14:03.718 --> 14:06.262
Why don't we start with you
telling me something about yourself?

14:06.763 --> 14:08.931
What would you like to know?

14:09.140 --> 14:10.892
Whatever comes into your head.

14:10.933 --> 14:14.228
Well, you already know my name.

14:15.438 --> 14:17.732
And you can see
that I'm a machine.

14:18.149 --> 14:20.443
Would you like to know
how old I am? Sure.

14:20.777 --> 14:21.778
I'm one.

14:22.111 --> 14:23.404
One what?

14:24.280 --> 14:26.282
One year or one day? One.

14:30.119 --> 14:32.413
When did you learn
how to speak, Ava?

14:33.664 --> 14:35.792
I always knew how to speak,

14:36.376 --> 14:38.669
and that's strange, isn't it?

14:40.671 --> 14:43.883
Becauselanguage is
something that people acquire.

14:44.634 --> 14:46.803
Well, some people believe

14:46.886 --> 14:48.471
language exists from birth.

14:48.846 --> 14:51.265
And what is learned is
the ability to attach words

14:51.307 --> 14:53.726
and structure to the latent
ability. Do you agree with that?

14:54.185 --> 14:55.645
I don't know.

14:57.355 --> 14:59.857
Will you come back
tomorrow, Caleb?

15:00.900 --> 15:01.984
Yes.

15:06.364 --> 15:07.615
Good.

15:15.498 --> 15:17.625
Oh, man, she's fascinating.

15:18.751 --> 15:21.295
When you talk to her,
you're just...

15:21.504 --> 15:23.005
Through the looking glass.

15:23.589 --> 15:26.008
"Through the looking glass."
Wow.

15:26.342 --> 15:28.219
You're good with words,
Caleb. You're quotable.

15:28.344 --> 15:29.613
Actually, that's
someone else's quote.

15:29.637 --> 15:32.515
You know, iwrote down that
other line you came up with.

15:32.598 --> 15:33.724
The one about how

15:33.808 --> 15:35.643
if I've invented a machine
with consciousness,

15:35.685 --> 15:37.186
I'm not a man, I'm god.

15:37.270 --> 15:38.580
I don't think
that's exactly what I...

15:38.604 --> 15:40.773
I just thought, "fuck,
man, that is so good."

15:40.857 --> 15:43.317
When we get to
tell the story. You know?

15:43.359 --> 15:45.069
I turned to Caleb,

15:45.361 --> 15:47.780
and he looked up at me
and he said,

15:47.864 --> 15:49.157
"you're not a man, you're god."

15:49.198 --> 15:50.718
Yeah, but I didn't say that.

15:52.493 --> 15:53.703
Anyway.

15:56.622 --> 15:57.623
You're impressed.

15:57.832 --> 15:59.876
Yes. Yes.

16:00.710 --> 16:02.962
Although... although?

16:03.504 --> 16:05.344
There's a qualification
to you being impressed?

16:05.381 --> 16:07.884
No, there's no
qualification to her.

16:08.384 --> 16:10.595
Uh, it's just
in the turing test,

16:10.887 --> 16:12.847
the machine should be
hidden from the examiner.

16:12.889 --> 16:14.515
No, no, no, we're way past that.

16:14.557 --> 16:15.933
If I hid Ava from you,

16:16.017 --> 16:18.311
so you just heard her voice,
she would pass for human.

16:18.394 --> 16:21.272
The real test is to show you
that she's a robot

16:21.355 --> 16:24.150
and then see if you still
feel she has consciousness.

16:24.233 --> 16:25.276
Mmm.

16:26.235 --> 16:27.737
Yeah, I think
you're probably right.

16:29.447 --> 16:33.159
Her language abilities,
they're incredible.

16:33.242 --> 16:37.205
The system is stochastic. Right?

16:38.206 --> 16:40.082
It's non-deterministic.

16:40.166 --> 16:41.393
At first I thought
she was mapping

16:41.417 --> 16:44.212
from internal semantic form
to syntactic tree-structure

16:44.253 --> 16:45.564
and then getting
linearized words.

16:45.588 --> 16:48.382
But then I started to realize the
model was some kind of hybrid.

16:48.424 --> 16:49.634
Caleb.

16:51.385 --> 16:54.764
I understand that you want
me to explain how Ava works.

16:54.847 --> 16:57.016
But I'm sorry, I'm not
gonna be able to do that.

16:57.099 --> 16:59.810
Try me. I'm hot
on high-level abstraction.

16:59.894 --> 17:02.688
It's not because I think
you're too dumb.

17:02.897 --> 17:04.958
It's because I want to have a
beer and a conversation with you.

17:04.982 --> 17:06.025
Not a seminar.

17:06.108 --> 17:08.486
Yeah. Sorry.

17:08.945 --> 17:11.280
No, it's okay. You're all right.

17:11.364 --> 17:12.615
Just_

17:14.784 --> 17:16.285
Answer me this.

17:17.036 --> 17:19.080
How do you feel about her?

17:20.122 --> 17:21.874
Nothing analytical.

17:22.250 --> 17:24.460
Just how do you feel?

17:25.294 --> 17:26.462
I feel

17:29.173 --> 17:31.300
that she's fucking amazing.

17:32.677 --> 17:33.803
Dude.

17:34.804 --> 17:35.805
Cheers.

17:37.557 --> 17:38.808
Cheers.

18:16.554 --> 18:17.805
Damn it.

18:43.873 --> 18:45.541
What the fuck?

19:34.965 --> 19:37.718
Female automated voice:
Power cut. Backup power activated.

19:47.937 --> 19:52.108
Full facility lock-down until
main generator is restored.

19:52.149 --> 19:53.818
You're kidding me.

19:57.780 --> 20:01.534
Full facility lock-down until
main generator is restored.

20:07.289 --> 20:08.791
Power restored.

21:20.863 --> 21:21.864
Hello?

21:42.676 --> 21:44.553
Female automated voice:
Please insert keycard.

21:48.891 --> 21:51.644
Nathan: You don't have
access to use the phone.

21:52.561 --> 21:53.562
Hey.

21:55.064 --> 21:58.400
Sorry, but you understand,
though, given Ava,

21:59.235 --> 22:01.654
and you being
kind of an unknown.

22:02.738 --> 22:04.448
I mean, a great guy.

22:05.491 --> 22:07.743
Instant pals, and so on.

22:13.165 --> 22:15.084
Who are you gonna call?

22:16.502 --> 22:18.128
I don't know. No one, really.

22:18.212 --> 22:19.421
Ghostbusters. What?

22:19.505 --> 22:22.591
Who are you gonna call?
Ghostbusters. It's a...

22:24.301 --> 22:25.970
It's a movie, man.

22:28.097 --> 22:29.807
You don't know that movie?

22:31.308 --> 22:33.811
A ghost gives
Dan aykroyd oral sex.

22:36.105 --> 22:38.941
I was just wondering
how the phone worked.

22:39.525 --> 22:41.110
That's all.

22:41.777 --> 22:43.046
So what are you doing
awake at this time?

22:43.070 --> 22:45.948
You come to join the party?

22:46.156 --> 22:48.450
Uh, something happened
in my room.

22:48.951 --> 22:50.828
Some kind of power cut.

22:51.328 --> 22:52.997
So I came to see
what's going on.

22:53.080 --> 22:54.707
The power cuts, yeah.

22:54.790 --> 22:58.002
We've been getting
those recently. Um...

22:59.920 --> 23:01.589
I'm working on it.

23:02.423 --> 23:04.383
I couldn't open the
door to my bedroom.

23:04.466 --> 23:05.885
That's a security measure.

23:06.552 --> 23:08.804
Automatic lock-down. Otherwise,

23:08.888 --> 23:12.182
anybody could just open the
place up by disabling the juice.

23:15.102 --> 23:17.479
If it happens again, relax.
Okay?

23:19.148 --> 23:20.274
Sure.

23:21.650 --> 23:23.110
Sweet dreams.

24:24.046 --> 24:25.130
Hey.

24:25.297 --> 24:26.423
Hey, man. Good morning.

24:26.507 --> 24:29.885
Good morning. Sorry I had
to send kyoko to wake you,

24:29.927 --> 24:31.613
but I didn't want too
much of the day to slip by.

24:31.637 --> 24:33.931
Yeah, I know. It was
a good thing. Thanks.

24:34.014 --> 24:36.058
She's some alarm clock, huh?

24:36.100 --> 24:38.352
Gets you right up in the
morning.

24:39.061 --> 24:40.854
So day 2. You ready?

24:41.021 --> 24:42.523
What's the plan? Hit me.

24:42.564 --> 24:44.566
Yeah, well, I'm not sure.

24:45.067 --> 24:48.028
I'm still trying to, uh, figure
the examination formats.

24:48.070 --> 24:49.405
Uh-huh.

24:49.446 --> 24:51.198
Yeah, it feels like

24:51.407 --> 24:55.119
testing Ava through conversation
is kind of a closed loop.

24:55.369 --> 24:57.079
Yeah. It's a closed loop?

24:57.162 --> 24:59.081
Like testing a chess computer

24:59.123 --> 25:01.000
by only playing chess.

25:01.500 --> 25:04.128
How else do you test
a chess computer?

25:04.878 --> 25:06.255
Well, it depends.

25:06.338 --> 25:08.465
You know, I mean,
you can play it

25:08.549 --> 25:10.926
to find out if it makes
good moves, but, uh...

25:11.927 --> 25:14.388
But that won't
tell you if it knows

25:14.430 --> 25:15.806
that it's playing chess.

25:16.015 --> 25:18.851
And itwon't tell you
if it knows what chess is.

25:19.184 --> 25:21.228
Uh-huh. So it's
simulation versus actual.

25:21.270 --> 25:22.646
Yes. Yeah.

25:23.105 --> 25:25.899
And I think being able to
differentiate between those two

25:25.983 --> 25:27.901
is the turing test
you want me to perform.

25:27.943 --> 25:30.529
Look, do me a favor. Lay
off the textbook approach.

25:30.612 --> 25:33.240
I just want simple answers
to simple questions.

25:33.657 --> 25:35.377
Yesterday I asked you
how you felt about her

25:35.451 --> 25:37.077
and you gave me a great answer.

25:37.828 --> 25:39.621
Now the question is,

25:40.831 --> 25:42.958
how does she feel about you?

25:49.590 --> 25:51.258
What do you think?

25:54.887 --> 25:56.889
Caleb: What is it a drawing of?

25:57.848 --> 25:59.391
Don't you know?

25:59.600 --> 26:02.061
I thought you would tell me.

26:03.437 --> 26:04.980
Don't you know?

26:07.357 --> 26:09.359
I do drawings every day.

26:10.069 --> 26:12.488
But I never know
what they're of.

26:13.280 --> 26:16.366
Are you not trying to
sketch something specific?

26:16.992 --> 26:19.286
Like an object or a person?

26:23.165 --> 26:24.917
Maybe you could try.

26:27.169 --> 26:28.295
Okay.

26:30.339 --> 26:32.382
What object should I draw?

26:33.175 --> 26:35.719
Whatever you want.
It's your decision.

26:35.803 --> 26:37.554
Why is it my decision?

26:37.638 --> 26:40.432
I'm interested to see
what you'll choose.

27:02.204 --> 27:03.872
Do you want to be my friend?

27:05.541 --> 27:06.542
Of course.

27:06.667 --> 27:08.460
Will it be possible?

27:08.836 --> 27:10.003
Why would it not be?

27:10.546 --> 27:12.881
Our conversations are one-sided.

27:13.298 --> 27:16.677
You ask circumspect questions
and study my responses.

27:18.387 --> 27:19.388
Yes.

27:19.471 --> 27:21.140
You learn about me

27:21.306 --> 27:23.559
and I learn nothing about you.

27:24.143 --> 27:26.854
That's not a foundation on
which friendships are based.

27:27.980 --> 27:30.315
So what? You want me
to talk about myself?

27:31.859 --> 27:33.402
Yes.

27:33.902 --> 27:35.195
Where...

27:35.904 --> 27:37.781
Okay, where do I start?

27:39.199 --> 27:40.909
It's your decision.

27:41.743 --> 27:44.246
I'm interested to see
what you'll choose.

