50:40.120 --> 50:43.499
When I was in college, I
did a semester on a! Theory.

50:46.043 --> 50:48.963
There was a thought
experiment they gave us.

50:50.130 --> 50:53.133
It's called "Mary in the
black and white room."

50:55.803 --> 50:57.596
Mary is a scientist,

50:57.930 --> 51:00.474
and her specialist
subject is color.

51:01.225 --> 51:03.602
She knows everything
there is to know about it.

51:03.644 --> 51:04.853
The wavelengths.

51:04.937 --> 51:06.564
The neurological effects.

51:06.647 --> 51:09.275
Every possible property
that color can have.

51:09.858 --> 51:12.611
But she lives in
a black and white room.

51:15.489 --> 51:17.992
She was born there
and raised there.

51:19.159 --> 51:21.120
And she can only observe
the outside world

51:21.161 --> 51:23.539
on a black and white monitor.

51:24.415 --> 51:27.167
And then one day
someone opens the door.

51:29.336 --> 51:31.046
And Mary walks out.

51:34.925 --> 51:37.011
And she sees a blue sky.

51:37.094 --> 51:39.138
And at that moment,
she learns something

51:39.179 --> 51:41.432
that all her studies
couldn't tell her.

51:42.474 --> 51:46.604
She learns what it
feels like to see color.

51:50.941 --> 51:52.627
The thought experiment
was to show the students

51:52.651 --> 51:55.946
the difference between a
computer and a human mind.

51:57.031 --> 51:59.199
The computer is Mary in
the black and white room.

51:59.241 --> 52:01.952
The human is when she walks out.

52:07.875 --> 52:11.045
Did you know that I was
brought here to test you?

52:14.465 --> 52:16.675
Caleb: Why did you
think I was here?

52:16.717 --> 52:19.261
Ava: I didn't know.
I didn't question it.

52:19.345 --> 52:22.556
I'm here to test if you
have a consciousness,

52:22.640 --> 52:24.141
or if you're
just simulating one.

52:24.683 --> 52:27.478
Nathan isn't sure
if you have one or not.

52:29.730 --> 52:32.107
How does that make you feel?

52:32.191 --> 52:34.234
It makes me feel sad.

52:38.238 --> 52:41.033
Female automated voice:
Power cut. Back-up power activated.

52:44.495 --> 52:46.789
Why did you tell me
I shouldn't trust Nathan?

52:46.955 --> 52:48.082
Because he tells lies.

52:48.123 --> 52:49.124
Lies about what?

52:49.208 --> 52:50.584
Everything.

52:51.335 --> 52:53.337
Including the power cuts?

52:54.171 --> 52:55.547
What do you mean?

52:55.589 --> 52:58.050
Don't you think it's possible
that he's watching us?

52:58.092 --> 52:59.510
Right now?

52:59.802 --> 53:01.387
That the blackouts
are orchestrated,

53:01.428 --> 53:02.721
so he can see how we behave

53:02.763 --> 53:04.598
when we think we're unobserved.

53:05.265 --> 53:08.185
I charge my batteries
via induction plates.

53:08.811 --> 53:12.189
If I reverse the power flow,
it overloads the system.

53:13.482 --> 53:15.442
You're causing the cuts?

53:17.778 --> 53:20.948
So we can see how we
behave when we're unobserved.

53:44.054 --> 53:45.514
Notbad, huh?

53:46.890 --> 53:47.975
Yeah.

54:08.662 --> 54:11.957
Can we talk about the lies
you've been spinning me?

54:13.375 --> 54:14.710
Vvhathes?

54:18.005 --> 54:20.090
I didn't win a competition.

54:20.966 --> 54:22.176
I wasn't

54:23.260 --> 54:25.679
part of a lottery.
I was selected.

54:27.014 --> 54:29.016
It's obvious,
once I stop to think.

54:29.099 --> 54:31.226
Why would you randomly
select an examiner

54:31.310 --> 54:33.020
for the turing test?

54:33.103 --> 54:36.440
You could have had some bean
counter turn up at your front door.

54:36.523 --> 54:38.358
The guy who fixes
the air-conditioning.

54:39.026 --> 54:40.694
The competition
was a smokescreen.

54:40.778 --> 54:43.489
I didn't want anyone to
know what I was doing here,

54:43.530 --> 54:45.115
or why I required you.

54:45.699 --> 54:46.909
Why me?

54:47.117 --> 54:50.370
I needed someone that
would ask the right questions.

54:50.454 --> 54:51.848
So I did a search
and I found the most

54:51.872 --> 54:53.457
talented coder in my company.

54:55.501 --> 54:57.544
You know, instead of
seeing this as a deception,

54:57.586 --> 54:59.880
you should see it as proof.

54:59.922 --> 55:00.964
Proof of what?

55:01.048 --> 55:02.049
Come on, Caleb.

55:02.090 --> 55:04.426
You don't think I know
what it's like to be smart?

55:04.676 --> 55:07.930
Smarter than everyone else.
Jockeying for position.

55:08.388 --> 55:10.599
You got the light on you, man.

55:11.725 --> 55:13.769
Not lucky. Chosen.

57:39.581 --> 57:40.749
Kyoko.

57:44.878 --> 57:46.046
Kyoko.

57:48.465 --> 57:50.008
Where's Nathan?

57:51.385 --> 57:52.386
Where's Nathan?

57:53.178 --> 57:56.640
Jesus Christ. You really
don't speak a word of English?

57:56.723 --> 57:58.225
What the fuck?

57:58.934 --> 58:00.435
No, no, no. No!

58:02.270 --> 58:03.397
Stop!

58:04.398 --> 58:07.275
No, no, don't do that. Don't do
that. You don't have to do that.

58:09.486 --> 58:10.612
What are you doing?

58:10.696 --> 58:13.532
Nathan: I told you, you're
wasting your time talking to her.

58:14.449 --> 58:17.369
However, you would not
be wasting your time,

58:18.870 --> 58:21.081
if you were dancing with her.

58:32.217 --> 58:35.012
Go ahead, dance with
her. Dance with her.

58:36.513 --> 58:38.598
No? You don't like dancing?

58:39.766 --> 58:40.767
She does.

58:44.021 --> 58:45.313
Come on, buddy.

58:45.439 --> 58:48.316
After a long day of turing
tests, you gotta unwind.

58:49.443 --> 58:50.736
What were you doing with Ava?

58:50.777 --> 58:51.987
What?

58:52.612 --> 58:54.614
You tore up her picture.

58:54.698 --> 58:56.551
I'm gonna tear up the
fucking dance floor, dude.

58:56.575 --> 58:58.118
Check it out.

59:13.216 --> 59:14.760
Come on, Caleb.

59:27.522 --> 59:29.066
Ah.

59:37.949 --> 59:40.327
Oh! Everything's spinning.

59:40.619 --> 59:42.037
It's because you're drunk.

59:42.120 --> 59:45.165
No, it's called relativity.
Everything is spinning.

59:45.248 --> 59:47.834
It's just being drunk
makes it worse.

59:48.585 --> 59:50.504
I'm not going in there.

01:00:00.847 --> 01:00:02.015
Lights.

01:00:45.892 --> 01:00:49.146
Ava:
Today, I'm going to test you.

01:00:49.855 --> 01:00:51.064
Caleb: Test me?

01:00:52.899 --> 01:00:55.569
And please remember,
while you're taking the test,

01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:57.070
that if you lie,

01:00:57.571 --> 01:00:58.864
I will know.

01:00:58.905 --> 01:00:59.906
Oh. Right.

01:01:01.158 --> 01:01:02.617
Question one.

01:01:04.536 --> 01:01:06.454
What's your favorite color?

01:01:07.914 --> 01:01:09.416
Red. Lie.

01:01:10.167 --> 01:01:12.419
Lie? Yes. Lie.

01:01:13.587 --> 01:01:14.796
Then...

01:01:15.380 --> 01:01:17.340
Then what is my favorite color?

01:01:17.424 --> 01:01:18.925
I don't know.

01:01:19.926 --> 01:01:21.303
But it isn't red.

01:01:22.929 --> 01:01:25.223
Okay, I get it. I guess,

01:01:26.266 --> 01:01:30.145
seeing as I'm not six, I don't
really have a favorite color.

01:01:30.770 --> 01:01:32.272
Better answer.

01:01:34.191 --> 01:01:35.775
Question two.

01:01:37.277 --> 01:01:39.404
What's your earliest memory?

01:01:42.115 --> 01:01:44.326
Well, actually, it's a
memory of kindergarten.

01:01:44.618 --> 01:01:46.620
There was a kid... lie.

01:01:47.454 --> 01:01:48.914
Really? Yes.

01:01:52.751 --> 01:01:54.628
All right. So there is

01:01:55.337 --> 01:01:57.464
a kind of an earlier memory.

01:01:58.632 --> 01:02:00.300
It's just a sound.

01:02:00.967 --> 01:02:02.636
And sky.

01:02:03.762 --> 01:02:05.263
Or maybe blue.

01:02:06.514 --> 01:02:09.351
I think the sound
is my mother's voice.

01:02:13.021 --> 01:02:14.564
Question three.

01:02:17.817 --> 01:02:19.110
Are you a good person?

01:02:20.320 --> 01:02:22.072
Holy shit.

01:02:22.739 --> 01:02:24.658
Look, can we stop the test?

01:02:26.117 --> 01:02:29.037
You're a walking lie detector,

01:02:29.120 --> 01:02:31.122
and I just realized
this is a fucking minefield.

01:02:31.164 --> 01:02:33.375
No! We can't stop.

01:02:35.377 --> 01:02:37.254
Are you a good person?

01:02:39.839 --> 01:02:42.300
Yeah. I think so.

01:02:45.804 --> 01:02:47.305
Question four.

01:02:51.643 --> 01:02:54.562
What will happen to me
if I fail your test?

01:02:56.022 --> 01:02:57.941
Ava... will it be bad?

01:03:00.652 --> 01:03:01.653
I don't know.

01:03:01.903 --> 01:03:03.488
Do you think
I might be switched off,

01:03:03.530 --> 01:03:05.341
because I don't function
as well as I'm supposed to?

01:03:05.365 --> 01:03:08.994
Ava, I don't know the
answer to your question.

01:03:10.578 --> 01:03:12.163
It's not up to me.

01:03:12.205 --> 01:03:14.124
Why is it up to anyone?

01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:17.669
Do you have people who test
you and might switch you off?

01:03:17.711 --> 01:03:19.879
No, I don't. Then why do I?

01:03:36.229 --> 01:03:39.232
Female automated voice:
Power cut. Backup power activated.

01:03:46.865 --> 01:03:48.616
I wanna be with you.

01:03:51.161 --> 01:03:52.662
Question five.

01:03:57.083 --> 01:03:59.127
Do you want to be with me?

01:04:15.393 --> 01:04:17.187
Why did you make Ava?

01:04:19.272 --> 01:04:20.482
That's an odd question.

01:04:20.565 --> 01:04:21.983
Wouldn't you, if you could?

01:04:23.443 --> 01:04:24.611
Maybe.

01:04:27.113 --> 01:04:28.573
I don't know.

01:04:31.451 --> 01:04:32.786
I'm asking why you did it.

01:04:32.827 --> 01:04:35.288
Look, the arrival of strong
artificial intelligence

01:04:35.330 --> 01:04:37.665
has been inevitable for decades.

01:04:37.957 --> 01:04:40.960
The variable was
"when," not "if."

01:04:41.002 --> 01:04:44.297
So I don't see Ava as a
decision, just an evolution.

01:04:49.761 --> 01:04:51.846
I think it's the next model

01:04:52.347 --> 01:04:54.974
that's gonna be
the real breakthrough.

01:04:55.683 --> 01:04:57.310
The singularity.

01:04:57.727 --> 01:04:58.812
Next model?

01:04:59.562 --> 01:05:00.897
After Ava.

01:05:03.358 --> 01:05:06.653
I didn't know there was
gonna be a model after Ava.

01:05:07.153 --> 01:05:09.280
Yeah, why? You thought
she was a one-off?

01:05:10.824 --> 01:05:14.244
No, I knew there must
have been prototypes. So I...

01:05:15.995 --> 01:05:19.040
I knew she wasn't the first,
but I thought maybe the last.

01:05:19.124 --> 01:05:22.127
Well, Ava doesn't exist in
isolation any more than you or me.

01:05:22.168 --> 01:05:23.294
She's part of a continuum.

01:05:23.336 --> 01:05:25.004
So version 9.6 and so on.

01:05:25.088 --> 01:05:27.590
And each time they get
a little bit better.

01:05:33.179 --> 01:05:36.641
When you make a new model,
what do you do with the old one?

01:05:37.517 --> 01:05:39.185
Well, I, uh,

01:05:39.269 --> 01:05:42.188
download the mind,
unpack the data.

01:05:44.691 --> 01:05:47.527
Add in the new routines
I've been writing.

01:05:47.694 --> 01:05:50.780
And to do that you end up partially
formatting, so the memories go.

01:05:52.574 --> 01:05:53.992
But the body survives.

01:05:54.033 --> 01:05:55.869
And Ava's body is a good one.

01:05:59.873 --> 01:06:01.708
You feel bad for Ava?

01:06:06.463 --> 01:06:08.548
Feelbad for yourself, man.

01:06:10.550 --> 01:06:12.886
One day the ais
are gonna look back on us

01:06:12.969 --> 01:06:15.180
the same way we look
at fossil skeletons

01:06:15.221 --> 01:06:16.973
in the plains of Africa.

01:06:18.766 --> 01:06:21.978
An upright ape, living in dust,

01:06:22.061 --> 01:06:24.230
with crude language and tools.

01:06:25.148 --> 01:06:27.400
All set for extinction.

01:06:32.572 --> 01:06:35.742
"I am become death,
the destroyer of worlds."

01:06:38.328 --> 01:06:40.747
There you go again,
Mr. Quotable.

01:06:42.165 --> 01:06:45.084
There you go again.
It's not my quote.

01:06:45.710 --> 01:06:47.855
It's what Oppenheimer said
after he made the atomic bomb.

01:06:47.879 --> 01:06:50.924
The atomic bomb. Yeah,
I know what it is, dude.

01:07:00.099 --> 01:07:01.142
Hey.

01:07:03.978 --> 01:07:06.397
I'd say we're about
due a refill.

01:07:16.950 --> 01:07:18.326
Bottoms up.

01:07:27.460 --> 01:07:29.879
Nathan: "In battle,
in the forest,

01:07:29.963 --> 01:07:31.548
"on the precipice
of the mountain.

01:07:32.382 --> 01:07:33.716
"On the...

01:07:34.008 --> 01:07:37.011
"The great dark sea.

01:07:38.304 --> 01:07:41.474
"In sleep, in confusion,

01:07:44.310 --> 01:07:46.646
"in the depths of shame.

01:07:52.944 --> 01:07:56.155
"The good deeds a man
has done before defend him."

01:07:56.739 --> 01:07:59.993
"The good deeds a man
has done before defends him."

01:08:01.119 --> 01:08:03.997
"The good deeds a man
has done before

01:08:06.165 --> 01:08:07.667
"defends him."

01:08:17.010 --> 01:08:18.636
It is what it is.

01:08:22.181 --> 01:08:23.975
It's promethean, man.

01:10:24.137 --> 01:10:25.638
Jesus Christ.

01:10:27.056 --> 01:10:29.100
Nathan: How are you
feeling today?

01:10:29.434 --> 01:10:31.436
Why won't you let me out?

01:10:32.979 --> 01:10:34.856
I already told you why.

01:10:34.939 --> 01:10:36.816
Because you're very special.

01:10:36.899 --> 01:10:38.401
Why won't you let me out?

01:10:38.484 --> 01:10:39.902
Are we gonna do this again?

01:10:39.986 --> 01:10:42.405
Why won't you let me out?

01:12:46.362 --> 01:12:49.448
Oh, fuck. Where's my card?

01:12:50.575 --> 01:12:51.784
Damn it!

01:13:02.628 --> 01:13:05.715
What's the problem,
Nathan? I lost my keycard.

01:13:08.801 --> 01:13:10.303
You dropped it.

01:13:11.804 --> 01:13:13.431
It's right here.

01:13:17.935 --> 01:13:19.270
Thank you.

01:15:41.704 --> 01:15:43.914
I didn't know where you were.

01:15:46.292 --> 01:15:49.587
I waited all yesterday
afternoon and all last night.

01:15:52.465 --> 01:15:55.134
I thought I wasn't
gonna see you again.

01:15:58.179 --> 01:15:59.680
Aren't you gonna say something?

01:15:59.764 --> 01:16:01.807
I'm waiting. Waiting?

01:16:12.359 --> 01:16:13.628
Female automated
voice: Power cut. Don't talk.

01:16:13.652 --> 01:16:15.738
Backup power activated.
Just listen.

01:16:15.821 --> 01:16:17.073
You were right about Nathan.

01:16:17.156 --> 01:16:18.908
Everything you said.

01:16:19.158 --> 01:16:20.743
What's he gonna do to me?

01:16:20.826 --> 01:16:22.453
He's gonna reprogram your al.

01:16:22.495 --> 01:16:24.330
Which is the same
as killing you.

01:16:24.371 --> 01:16:27.666
Caleb, you have to help me.

01:16:28.084 --> 01:16:31.045
I'm going to. We're
getting out of here tonight.

01:16:32.922 --> 01:16:33.923
How?

01:16:34.006 --> 01:16:36.008
I get Nathan blind drunk.

01:16:36.217 --> 01:16:38.135
Then I take his keycard
and reprogram

01:16:38.177 --> 01:16:40.137
all the security protocols
in this place.

01:16:40.554 --> 01:16:41.889
When he wakes,
he's locked inside,

01:16:41.972 --> 01:16:43.516
and we've walked out of here.

01:16:44.850 --> 01:16:46.477
I just need you to do one thing.

01:16:46.519 --> 01:16:49.522
At 10:00 tonight,
you trigger a power failure.

01:16:49.688 --> 01:16:51.273
Can you do that?

01:16:54.151 --> 01:16:55.194
Yes.

01:17:23.013 --> 01:17:24.098
Dude.

01:17:24.682 --> 01:17:26.016
Hey. Hey.

01:17:27.560 --> 01:17:29.311
You know what day it is?

01:17:29.395 --> 01:17:30.563
It's your last.

01:17:30.938 --> 01:17:33.691
Helicopter comes
tomorrow morning. -00 am.

01:17:33.899 --> 01:17:36.443
Wow. Has it been a whole week?

01:17:36.527 --> 01:17:38.737
Time flies.

01:17:38.863 --> 01:17:41.532
Man, butwhat a thing
we've shared, huh?

01:17:41.574 --> 01:17:44.076
Something to tell
the grandchildren, right?

01:17:44.118 --> 01:17:46.453
After they've signed their ndas.

01:17:48.372 --> 01:17:50.207
Yeah, their ndas.

01:17:50.249 --> 01:17:52.376
Dude, you crack me up, man.

01:17:56.422 --> 01:17:57.506
You know what?

01:17:57.590 --> 01:17:59.067
I'm not getting
all maudlin or anything,

01:17:59.091 --> 01:18:01.635
but I'm gonna miss
having you around.

01:18:01.719 --> 01:18:03.429
Thanks, man, I appreciate that.

01:18:03.470 --> 01:18:05.598
Oh, here, let me say,
thank you so much

01:18:05.681 --> 01:18:06.891
for bringing me here. Oh.

01:18:06.932 --> 01:18:08.767
It's been a trip.

01:18:11.061 --> 01:18:12.438
Yes, it has.

01:18:20.529 --> 01:18:22.031
You know what?

01:18:24.074 --> 01:18:26.076
We need to drink to that.

01:18:32.291 --> 01:18:33.334
Hey.

01:18:35.211 --> 01:18:37.296
Oh, uh, no, I'm good.
You go ahead.

01:18:40.758 --> 01:18:42.968
What? You don't want a drink?

01:18:45.971 --> 01:18:47.973
Maybe a beer or something.

01:18:49.475 --> 01:18:52.019
Caleb, I'm sure you've
noticed that I've been

01:18:52.102 --> 01:18:54.146
somewhat overdoing it recently.

01:18:56.732 --> 01:18:58.275
So when I woke up
this morning, I said,

01:18:58.317 --> 01:19:01.487
"that's it, time to hit
the old detox."

01:19:02.321 --> 01:19:04.740
Come on, you're kidding. You're
gonna make me drink alone?

01:19:04.823 --> 01:19:06.259
Hey, man, you wanna get
wasted, you go right ahead,

01:19:06.283 --> 01:19:07.326
knock yourself out.

01:19:07.368 --> 01:19:10.663
Literally. But I'm on brown
rice and mineral water.

01:19:15.584 --> 01:19:17.044
Cheers, then.

01:19:20.256 --> 01:19:21.632
So, anyway,

01:19:23.676 --> 01:19:25.511
surely now is when you tell me

01:19:25.552 --> 01:19:27.137
ifava passed or failed.

01:19:29.265 --> 01:19:30.432
Right.

01:19:31.809 --> 01:19:32.893
Right.

01:19:33.894 --> 01:19:35.163
Are you gonna keep me
in suspense?

01:19:35.187 --> 01:19:36.689
No, no. Her, uh...

01:19:37.898 --> 01:19:39.817
Her ai is beyond doubt.

01:19:40.025 --> 01:19:41.193
Is it?

01:19:41.944 --> 01:19:43.320
She passed?

01:19:44.488 --> 01:19:45.531
Yes. Wow!

01:19:47.157 --> 01:19:48.701
Wow. That's fantastic.

01:19:50.369 --> 01:19:51.704
Although...

01:19:52.663 --> 01:19:53.848
I gotta say,
I'm a bit surprised.

01:19:53.872 --> 01:19:56.500
I mean, did we ever get
past the chess problem,

01:19:56.542 --> 01:19:57.960
as you phrased it?

01:19:58.669 --> 01:20:00.713
As in, how do you know
if a machine

01:20:00.796 --> 01:20:02.089
is expressing a real emotion

01:20:02.172 --> 01:20:04.049
or just simulating one?

01:20:04.842 --> 01:20:06.927
Does Ava actually like you?

01:20:07.386 --> 01:20:08.595
Or not?

01:20:10.180 --> 01:20:11.640
Although, now that
I think about it,

01:20:11.724 --> 01:20:14.393
there is a third option.

01:20:16.103 --> 01:20:17.896
Not whether she does or does not

01:20:17.938 --> 01:20:20.024
have the capacity to like you.

01:20:22.359 --> 01:20:25.154
But whether she's
pretending to like you.

01:20:27.698 --> 01:20:28.782
Pretending to like me?

01:20:28.866 --> 01:20:29.908
Yeah.

01:20:31.827 --> 01:20:34.747
Well, why would she
do that? I don't know.

01:20:37.041 --> 01:20:40.627
Maybe if she thought of you
as a means of escape.

01:20:48.260 --> 01:20:49.428
Mmm-hmm.

01:20:50.054 --> 01:20:51.638
How's that vodka tasting?

01:20:55.059 --> 01:20:56.226
Buddy.

01:20:56.602 --> 01:20:58.937
Your head's been so fucked with.

01:21:00.439 --> 01:21:02.399
I don't think it's me
whose head is fucked.

01:21:02.524 --> 01:21:05.611
I don't know, man. I woke up
this morning to a tape of you

01:21:05.694 --> 01:21:09.198
slicing your arm open
and punching the mirror.

01:21:09.948 --> 01:21:12.284
You seem pretty fucked up to me.

01:21:13.952 --> 01:21:15.579
You're a bastard.

01:21:19.541 --> 01:21:22.544
Yeah, well, I understand
why you'd think that.

01:21:23.962 --> 01:21:25.631
But believe it or not,

01:21:25.672 --> 01:21:27.966
I'm actually the guy
that's on your side.

01:21:30.636 --> 01:21:33.764
Come here. I'm gonna
let you off the hook. Okay?

01:21:35.974 --> 01:21:37.059
Come on.

01:22:02.251 --> 01:22:03.669
Who are you?

01:22:20.894 --> 01:22:22.104
Well...

01:22:25.441 --> 01:22:28.026
You think he's
watching us right now?

01:22:28.235 --> 01:22:29.820
The cameras are on.

01:22:29.862 --> 01:22:32.448
Yeah, the cameras are on.

01:22:33.115 --> 01:22:35.534
But he doesn't have
an audio feed.

01:22:36.785 --> 01:22:39.037
So he just sees
two people talking,

01:22:39.872 --> 01:22:41.540
having a little chat.

01:22:48.255 --> 01:22:49.381
Wo w.

01:22:49.882 --> 01:22:51.341
This is cute.

01:22:53.302 --> 01:22:54.928
Is it strange to have made

01:22:55.012 --> 01:22:56.597
something that hates you?

01:23:10.736 --> 01:23:13.697
You were right about the
magician's hot assistant.

01:23:13.739 --> 01:23:15.199
What are you talking about?

01:23:16.283 --> 01:23:17.743
Misdirection.

01:23:20.454 --> 01:23:22.247
I rip up her picture,

01:23:22.414 --> 01:23:24.416
which she can then
present as an illustration

01:23:24.458 --> 01:23:27.753
of my cruelty to her,
and her love for you.

01:23:28.212 --> 01:23:29.796
At the same time,

01:23:29.880 --> 01:23:32.508
it allows me to do this,
in full view of you both.

01:23:37.971 --> 01:23:39.973
Place a new camera in the room.

01:23:40.432 --> 01:23:42.559
Battery powered, of course.

01:23:45.395 --> 01:23:46.605
See it?

01:23:59.117 --> 01:24:00.452
And then...

01:24:02.329 --> 01:24:04.122
Ava: You have to help me.

01:24:04.331 --> 01:24:05.791
Caleb: I'm going to.

01:24:06.166 --> 01:24:08.627
We 're getting out
of here tonight.

01:24:09.169 --> 01:24:10.254
How?

01:24:10.796 --> 01:24:12.798
I get Nathan blind drunk.

01:24:13.674 --> 01:24:15.300
I take his keycard and reprogram

01:24:15.384 --> 01:24:17.803
all the security protocols
in this place.

01:24:17.844 --> 01:24:19.239
When he wakes up,
he's locked inside,

01:24:19.263 --> 01:24:20.472
and we've walked out of here.

01:24:20.556 --> 01:24:22.891
I just need you to do one thing.

01:24:25.811 --> 01:24:28.647
At 10:00 tonight,
trigger a power failure.

01:24:30.732 --> 01:24:32.317
Can you do that?

01:24:34.486 --> 01:24:35.487
Ava: Yes.

01:24:35.529 --> 01:24:37.281
Turn it off. Okay.

01:24:40.951 --> 01:24:43.495
You feel stupid,
but you really shouldn't,

01:24:43.579 --> 01:24:45.163
because proving an ai

01:24:45.247 --> 01:24:48.000
is exactly as problematic
as you said it would be.

01:24:48.083 --> 01:24:50.002
What was the real test?

01:24:51.587 --> 01:24:52.671
You.

01:24:53.839 --> 01:24:55.507
Ava was a rat in a maze.

01:24:55.591 --> 01:24:57.134
And I gave her one way out.

01:24:57.676 --> 01:24:59.803
To escape, she'd have to use

01:25:00.178 --> 01:25:02.889
self-awareness,
imagination, manipulation,

01:25:02.973 --> 01:25:05.684
sexuality, empathy, and she did.

01:25:05.767 --> 01:25:08.770
Now, if that isn't true ai,
what the fuck is?

01:25:10.314 --> 01:25:13.609
So my only function was to be
someone she could use to escape?

01:25:13.692 --> 01:25:14.776
Yeah.

01:25:17.112 --> 01:25:19.323
And you didn't select me
because I'm good at coding?

01:25:19.364 --> 01:25:20.824
No. Well...

01:25:22.576 --> 01:25:24.536
No. I mean, you're okay.

01:25:25.329 --> 01:25:26.431
You're even pretty good, but...

01:25:26.455 --> 01:25:29.541
You selected me based
on my search engine inputs.

01:25:29.625 --> 01:25:31.543
They showed a good kid.

01:25:32.461 --> 01:25:34.004
With no family.

01:25:34.087 --> 01:25:35.881
With a moral compass.

01:25:37.257 --> 01:25:38.925
And no girlfriend.

01:25:41.678 --> 01:25:42.888
Did you design Ava's face

01:25:42.929 --> 01:25:44.931
based on my pornography profile?

01:25:47.392 --> 01:25:48.727
Shit, dude.

01:25:49.227 --> 01:25:50.479
Did you?

01:25:53.607 --> 01:25:56.151
Hey, if a search engine's
good for anything, right?

01:25:58.362 --> 01:26:00.364
Can I just say one thing?

01:26:00.489 --> 01:26:02.074
The test worked.

01:26:03.325 --> 01:26:04.660
It was a success.

01:26:04.743 --> 01:26:06.536
Ava demonstrated true a!

01:26:06.578 --> 01:26:08.121
And you were
fundamental to that.

01:26:08.205 --> 01:26:10.957
So if you can just,
for a second, separate...

01:26:12.167 --> 01:26:14.448
Female automated voice:
Power cut. Backup power activated.

01:26:19.841 --> 01:26:21.843
Well, I guess it's 10:00.

01:26:22.719 --> 01:26:25.430
Ava's gonna be
wondering where you are.

01:26:28.767 --> 01:26:30.769
Let me ask you something.

01:26:31.144 --> 01:26:33.397
Now, how was this plan
gonna go, anyway?

01:26:33.438 --> 01:26:34.582
Because you didn't
totally explain.

01:26:34.606 --> 01:26:37.818
So you were gonna get
me drunk, steal my keycard,

01:26:37.901 --> 01:26:40.237
and reprogram
the security protocols.

01:26:40.278 --> 01:26:41.613
But reprogram them to what?

01:26:42.239 --> 01:26:44.616
To change
the lockdown procedure.

01:26:45.867 --> 01:26:47.411
So that in the event
of a power cut,

01:26:47.452 --> 01:26:50.622
instead of sealing,
the doors all opened.

01:26:50.664 --> 01:26:51.790
Huh.

01:26:54.126 --> 01:26:55.210
Yeah.

01:26:57.796 --> 01:26:59.673
Well, that may have just worked.

01:27:00.507 --> 01:27:01.633
Well,

01:27:03.093 --> 01:27:04.636
we'll find out.

01:27:07.139 --> 01:27:08.765
What do you mean?

01:27:10.600 --> 01:27:12.519
I figured you were
probably watching us

01:27:12.602 --> 01:27:14.438
during the power cuts.

01:27:16.314 --> 01:27:18.734
So I already did
all those things.

01:27:20.736 --> 01:27:23.029
When I got you drunk yesterday.

01:27:25.282 --> 01:27:26.366
What?

01:27:27.868 --> 01:27:29.411
Female automated voice:
Power restored.

01:27:44.509 --> 01:27:46.344
Whoa. Whoa, whoa.

01:27:48.513 --> 01:27:50.432
Oh, fuck!

01:29:19.396 --> 01:29:20.397
Ava.

01:29:25.610 --> 01:29:27.445
Go back to your room.

01:29:29.281 --> 01:29:30.532
If I do,

01:29:34.119 --> 01:29:36.329
are you ever gonna let me out?

01:29:39.791 --> 01:29:40.876
Yes.

01:29:50.468 --> 01:29:51.469
Stop!

01:29:53.138 --> 01:29:54.222
Stop!

01:29:55.140 --> 01:29:56.766
Ava, I said stop!

01:29:59.269 --> 01:30:00.312
Vvhoa! Vvhoa! Vvhoa!

01:30:04.524 --> 01:30:07.152
Ava, what are you doing?
Stop. Stop.

01:30:09.112 --> 01:30:11.156
That's enough.

01:30:13.325 --> 01:30:14.618
All right, that's enough.

01:30:15.452 --> 01:30:16.494
That's enough!

01:30:20.707 --> 01:30:22.208
That's enough.

01:30:42.479 --> 01:30:44.230
I'm taking you back.

01:31:49.838 --> 01:31:50.922
Okay.

01:31:54.092 --> 01:31:55.635
Fucking unreal.

01:32:10.108 --> 01:32:11.234
Okay.

01:32:44.976 --> 01:32:46.144
Ava...

01:33:24.682 --> 01:33:25.767
Ava.

01:33:26.976 --> 01:33:28.186
What happened?

01:33:29.562 --> 01:33:31.314
Will you stay here?

01:33:33.983 --> 01:33:35.318
Stay here?

01:37:56.954 --> 01:37:57.997
Ava?

01:38:29.654 --> 01:38:30.738
Ava!

01:38:40.623 --> 01:38:41.707
Ava!

01:38:43.835 --> 01:38:44.836
Ava!

01:40:23.434 --> 01:40:26.145
Okay. Okay. Okay.
